      <h1>How Bitcoin&#39;s Difficulty Adjustment Works</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin&#39;s mainnet difficulty adjustment periodically recalculates the proof-of-work target from prior block timing. The ordinary rule changes the target only at 2,016-block boundaries, limits each adjustment, and aims for a long-run average spacing without scheduling blocks exactly ten minutes apart.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Mining</li><li>Deep</li><li>Technical Analysis</li><li>14 to 17 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-18</li></ul>
